"Cold storage tank discharge with phase change (MSTh R6 Ex4)

A 120 m3 water/ice thermal energy storage tank is discharged through a
glycol-water heat exchanger. Glycol mass flow rate: 90 kg/s, inlet T = 5 C.
Overall heat transfer coefficient AU = 0.5 MW/K. No heat loss to ambient.

The specific internal energy u [J/kg] of the water/ice mixture is integrated
over time. Phase-change logic tracks ice quality, water temperature, and
enthalpy during melting. Initial state: fully charged ice at -0.01 C.

Source: MSTh repetition exercise 4 (University of Liege thermal systems course).
"

"--- Tank and fluid data ---"
V_sto = 120
M_dot = 90
AU = 5E5
T_su = 5
c_p = 3800
P = 101325
M = V_sto * 1000

"--- Integration interval ---"
tau_1 = 0
tau_2 = 50000

"--- Energy balance ---"
Q_dot_env_sto = 0
U_dot_sto = M * u_dot
H_dot_br_sto = Q_dot_br_sto
Q_dot_br_sto = epsilon * M_dot * c_p * (T_su - T_w)
epsilon = 1 - exp(-NTU)
NTU = AU / C_dot
C_dot = M_dot * c_p

"--- Integrated states ---"
u = u_1 + INTEGRAL(u_dot, tau, 0, 50000)
"Total heat discharged to the glycol loop over the integration interval [J]"
E_discharged = INTEGRAL(Q_dot_br_sto, tau, 0, 50000)
u_1 = u_ice_0
"TEMPORARY: CoolProp INTENERGY(Water, T=-0.01, P=P) fails near the freezing
point (NaN in verification). Replace with the CoolProp call once that is fixed.
Same for VOLUME() below — use tabulated constants for now."
u_ice_0 = -333000
u_dot = U_dot_sto / M

"--- Phase-change temperatures and quality (nested 3-arg IF) ---"
t_ice_0 = -0.01
t_liq_0 = 0
u_liq_0 = 0
c_ice = 2200
c_liq = 4187
t_ice = t_ice_0 + (u - u_ice_0) / c_ice
t_liq = t_liq_0 + (u - u_liq_0) / c_liq
t_w = IF(u - u_ice_0, IF(u, t_liq, 0), t_ice)
t_melt = IF(-u - 1, t_liq_0, t_liq)
x_two_phase = (u - u_liq_0) / (u_ice_0 - u_liq_0)
x_ice = IF(u - u_ice_0, IF(u, 0, x_two_phase), 1)
x_melt = IF(u, 0, x_two_phase)
"TEMPORARY: replace with VOLUME(Water, T=t_ice_ref, P=P) and
VOLUME(Water, T=t_liq_ref, P=P) once CoolProp near-freezing evaluation works."
v_ice = 0.001091
v_liq = 0.001004
v = x_ice * v_ice + (1 - x_ice) * v_liq
DELTAU_sto = M * (u - u_1)

$IntegralTable tau:500 x_ice u t_w Q_dot_br_sto E_discharged t_melt v t_ice t_liq
